      "title": "Slash-less IANA ids other than UTC are rejected",
      "evidence": "IsKnownZone only accepts ids that contain '/' or equal \"UTC\". Valid IANA ids without a slash, such as \"Japan\", \"Egypt\" or \"EST5EDT\", get a 400 even though the tz data knows them. A browser would rarely report these, but the spec only says unknown zones are rejected and does not cover this case. I report it as minor for that reason. No reproduction is attached because it is below major.",
